Drop hero lifestyle photography here.

Homepage hero carousel (js/hero-carousel.js, SLIDES array):
  Now uses real, licensed photography hotlinked from Unsplash's CDN
  (free tier — Unsplash License, commercial use OK, no attribution
  required: https://unsplash.com/license), sized per-viewport via
  buildImageUrl() in that file. No local files are required for the
  carousel.

  If you'd rather self-host instead of hotlinking:
  1. Download the three photos referenced by `imageId` in the
     SLIDES array (open https://unsplash.com/photos/<imageId> for
     each, e.g. https://unsplash.com/photos/1643379850623-7eb6442cd262
     — note the ID in that URL differs slightly from the slug-style
     URLs Unsplash's UI shows; search images.unsplash.com/photo-<id>
     directly, or re-search Unsplash for the photographer names
     credited in hero-carousel.js).
  2. Save them here as carousel-slide-1.jpg / -2.jpg / -3.jpg.
  3. In hero-carousel.js, change buildImageUrl() to return
     `images/hero/carousel-slide-${n}.jpg` instead of building an
     Unsplash URL.

Also referenced elsewhere on the site:
  hero-lifestyle.jpg    — portrait, ~1000x1250px (About page preview)
Recommended tone throughout: warm, soft natural light.
